le, clothing, and stethoscope.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - retain his identity and clothing throughout his farewell and departure.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3], [Shot 4]): fully_preserved - retain furniture, daylight, desk-prop positions, and established spatial relationships.\n<Audio 1>: reference - retain the doctor's vocal identity and timbre during her affectionate phone conversation, adapting emotion without changing the speaker's voice; source dialogue and background sounds are not copied.\n<Audio 2>: reference - retain the patient's vocal identity and timbre during his polite farewell; source dialogue and background sounds are not copied.\n\ndetailed_description:\nContinue the same realistic live-action Chinese drama, 16:9, with matched daylight, color, character identities, and restrained performances. The doctor's voice remains tied to <Audio 1> as her delivery changes from clinical reserve to private warmth. The patient's voice remains tied to <Audio 2>. All dialogue is newly performed with synchronized Mandarin lip movement.\n\n[Shot 1] A medium close-up frames <Subject 2>, still seated in his slate-blue T-shirt, looking toward <Subject 1> off screen left. Her softly blurred white-coated shoulder remains at the left foreground edge. He briefly lowers his eyes, then looks back with a polite, accepting expression. <Subject 2> (S1), using the vocal identity and timbre of <Audio 2>, says with a brief hesitation after “那”: <d>[Chinese] 好吧，那……我先回去了，谢谢主任。</d> Complete the sentence by approximately 00:03.200. He then leans forward slightly to prepare to stand.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.500, the camera cuts to the established medium-wide two-shot of <Subject 3>, with <Subject 1> behind the desk on screen left and <Subject 2> on screen right. He rises naturally, moving the black chair backward a short distance with a subdued scrape. She gives one small silent nod and follows him with her eyes. He walks around his side of the desk and exits frame right by approximately 00:06.400. His footsteps recede toward the nearby exit. At approximately 00:06.600, the black smartphone on the doctor's side of the desk starts vibrating against the tabletop. She looks down toward it.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:07.200, the camera cuts to a tight desk-level insert of the vibrating phone beside the closed medical file. <Subject 1>'s right hand picks it up and taps once to answer. The vibration stops. Her right hand begins lifting the phone toward her ear, preserving the continuous physical action.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:08.300, the camera cuts to a medium close-up of <Subject 1> with the phone at her right ear. Her shoulders relax and her expression softens. <Subject 1> (S2), using the vocal identity and timbre of <Audio 1> with affectionate, familiar delivery, says: <d>[Chinese] 喂，老公……</d> During the short listening pause, she raises her left wrist and glances at her watch around 00:09.700–00:10.300. Keeping the phone at her right ear, <Subject 1> (S2) continues with the same timbre referenced from <Audio 1>: <d>[Chinese] 刚好下班，你等我一下。</d> Finish by approximately 00:12.800. She lowers her wrist and holds a small private smile while listening until 00:14.000. Her husband's voice is not audible.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nContinuous quiet room ambience supports the synchronized chair scrape, clothing movement, receding footsteps, phone vibration against the desk, and phone-handling sounds. Generate these physical sounds independently of the voice-reference recordings. Use no ringtone, audible caller response, added comedy effects, or music.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the female doctor from <Picture 1>, preserving her facial identity, low black hair bun, white medical coat, green scrubs, and stethoscope.\n<Subject 2> is the young adult male patient from <Picture 2>, preserving his facial identity, short textured black hair, slate-blue T-shi